accessWidener v2 named

# Access control for the 1.21.11 target.
#
# Prism's accessWidener(...) in the root build script is the only place this
# is declared; it feeds Fabric as-is and converts the same file into a NeoForge
# access transformer.
#
# The header above is the entire 1.21.11 -> 26.x difference. A 1.21.11 target is
# obfuscated and remapped by fabric-loom-remap, so it needs the "named"
# namespace. A 26.x target ships unobfuscated, where Loom expects "official" --
# which on 26.x is already the Mojang name, so the NeoForge conversion stays
# correct on both.
#
# The header must be line 1 and the separators must be spaces, for the same
# reasons as the 26.1 class tweaker: Loom reads the first line verbatim and
# Prism's converter is more forgiving than Loom's reader.

# --- Phase 2: block entity types -------------------------------------------
# 1.21.11 has no BlockEntityType.Builder either, and its construction routes
# are the same pair 26.1 has: a public static register(String, BlockEntitySupplier,
# Block...) and a private constructor
#
#   private BlockEntityType(BlockEntitySupplier<? extends T>, Set<Block>)
#
# The constructor is what gets widened rather than the static register, for the
# reason spelled out in the 26.x classtweaker: 26.2 deleted register outright,
# so an entry naming it cannot work on every target, whereas the constructor
# exists on all four with the same descriptor -- private on 1.21.11 and 26.1,
# already public on 26.2. Widening it is a no-op where it is already public.
accessible method net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType <init> (Lnet/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier;Ljava/util/Set;)V

# Unlike 26.1 and 26.2, this one is load-bearing here: 1.21.11 declares
# BlockEntitySupplier package-private, so the constructor stays unreachable
# until the type itself is widened. Matches "<T>BlockEntityType(BlockEntitySupplier
# <? extends T>,Set<Block>) has private access" at VanillaRegistrar.
accessible class net/minecraft/world/level/block/entity/BlockEntityType$BlockEntitySupplier
